WEBVTT

1
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.875
In verses 17.7 to 17.10 of Chapter 17,

2
00:01:01.875 --> 00:01:03.083
Lord Krishna explained

3
00:01:03.083 --> 00:01:06.541
that food too is influenced by the three gunas –

4
00:01:06.541 --> 00:01:08.291
and as the food is,

5
00:01:08.291 --> 00:01:12.541
so the direction of the mind
and consciousness becomes.

6
00:01:12.541 --> 00:01:15.958
Now in verses 17.11 to 17.13,

7
00:01:15.958 --> 00:01:19.083
He discusses yajna – sacrifice – which is one

8
00:01:19.083 --> 00:01:22.791
of the three main pillars of religious life,

9
00:01:22.791 --> 00:01:25.375
along with charity and austerity.

10
00:01:25.375 --> 00:01:27.125
In verses 17.2 to 17.4

11
00:01:27.125 --> 00:01:28.833
of the chapter, Lord Krishna

12
00:01:28.833 --> 00:01:33.458
had mentioned those people who,
due to laziness or difficulty,

13
00:01:33.458 --> 00:01:35.500
give up the scriptures,

14
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.500
yet worship with faith.

15
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:39.958
Now He shows –

16
00:01:39.958 --> 00:01:44.250
how yajna itself too is influenced by
the three gunas –

17
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.291
sattvic, rajasic, and tamasic.

18
00:01:47.291 --> 00:01:50.333
And that the very same religious act,

19
00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:51.500
according to its purpose,

20
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:52.875
attitude, and

21
00:01:52.875 --> 00:01:54.291
method,

22
00:01:54.291 --> 00:01:57.250
can either purify the seeker

23
00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.708
or lead them toward downfall.

24
00:02:05.666 --> 00:02:08.000
A person influenced by the sattvic quality

25
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.750
performs yajna with this feeling –

26
00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.500
‘This is my duty.

27
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.166
I have no hope of any reward.

28
00:02:15.166 --> 00:02:15.916
I simply

29
00:02:15.916 --> 00:02:19.291
follow the instructions of the scriptures.’

30
00:02:19.291 --> 00:02:22.041
Such a yajna is performed aphalakankshibhir –

31
00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:25.041
without the desire for fruit – and vidhi-dishta,

32
00:02:25.041 --> 00:02:28.208
that is, according to scripture.

33
00:02:28.208 --> 00:02:29.416
The mind is completely

34
00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:31.375
focused on the action,

35
00:02:31.375 --> 00:02:34.625
seeing it as a sacred act,

36
00:02:34.625 --> 00:02:37.333
not as a means of personal gain.

37
00:02:37.333 --> 00:02:40.166
As a result, this yajna brings purity,

38
00:02:40.166 --> 00:02:43.750
steadiness, and spiritual progress.

39
00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:48.208
But not every yajna is always like this.

40
00:02:48.208 --> 00:02:50.458
Lord Krishna warns that

41
00:02:50.458 --> 00:02:54.583
when a person performs yajna
only for material gain –

42
00:02:54.583 --> 00:02:56.916
such as to go to heaven,

43
00:02:56.916 --> 00:02:59.458
for good business results,

44
00:02:59.458 --> 00:03:02.083
or for public recognition –

45
00:03:02.083 --> 00:03:04.708
then it becomes rajasic.

46
00:03:04.708 --> 00:03:08.208
Here two tendencies dominate –

47
00:03:08.208 --> 00:03:11.625
phala-abhisandhi, that is, attraction toward

48
00:03:11.625 --> 00:03:14.666
results, and dambhartha, that is,

49
00:03:14.666 --> 00:03:17.708
the desire for name and fame.

50
00:03:17.708 --> 00:03:21.500
This yajna may be impressive on
the outside, but

51
00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.208
its inner purpose

52
00:03:23.208 --> 00:03:25.333
is self-centred.

53
00:03:25.333 --> 00:03:27.000
It is not sattvic,

54
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.041
it is rajasic, and it binds the person

55
00:03:30.041 --> 00:03:33.750
even more in the cycle of karma.

56
00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:37.250
Now comes the matter of tamasic yajna.

57
00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:40.750
When a yajna is performed turned away
from scripture, without

58
00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:44.583
distribution of food – asrishtanna,
without proper mantras –

59
00:03:44.583 --> 00:03:49.000
mantra-heen, without honouring
the priest – adakshinam,

60
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.583
and without faith,

61
00:03:51.583 --> 00:03:54.458
then it is considered tamasic.

62
00:03:54.458 --> 00:03:57.083
From the outside it may appear religious,

63
00:03:57.083 --> 00:03:58.166
but such actions

64
00:03:58.166 --> 00:04:02.000
have no real spiritual value.

65
00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.333
These may be superstition, fear,

66
00:04:04.333 --> 00:04:07.333
or harmful tendencies.

67
00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:09.791
This is the kind of religiosity that is without

68
00:04:09.791 --> 00:04:11.750
clarity or purpose –

69
00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:12.708
conduct carried out

70
00:04:12.708 --> 00:04:16.791
in the wrong direction by a confused mind.

71
00:04:16.791 --> 00:04:19.250
Through these verses, Lord Krishna

72
00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:21.916
teaches us that the action alone

73
00:04:21.916 --> 00:04:25.958
is not important, but the desire, the feeling,

74
00:04:25.958 --> 00:04:29.083
and the alignment with dharma decide

75
00:04:29.083 --> 00:04:33.541
whether an action is uplifting or degrading.

76
00:04:33.541 --> 00:04:37.000
Yajna is meaningful only when it is sincere,

77
00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.750
scripturally aligned, and selfless.

78
00:04:45.625 --> 00:04:48.625
You perform some sacred act –

79
00:04:48.625 --> 00:04:52.375
a fast, worship, a ritual – thinking

80
00:04:52.375 --> 00:04:55.291
that this is enough.

81
00:04:55.291 --> 00:04:57.041
But I want to ask you

82
00:04:57.041 --> 00:05:00.208
this question:

83
00:05:00.208 --> 00:05:03.125
what is the feeling behind it?

84
00:05:03.125 --> 00:05:06.875
Even the value of a divine act like

85
00:05:06.875 --> 00:05:10.125
yajna decreases when it is done

86
00:05:10.125 --> 00:05:12.583
without faith,

87
00:05:12.583 --> 00:05:14.750
without gratitude toward those

88
00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.458
who made it possible,

89
00:05:16.458 --> 00:05:20.958
and without the compassion to share it

90
00:05:20.958 --> 00:05:25.166
with others.

91
00:05:25.166 --> 00:05:28.833
If you offer something to Me, but

92
00:05:28.833 --> 00:05:33.208
show no love toward the people around you,

93
00:05:33.208 --> 00:05:36.541
then where has the real feeling of that offering

94
00:05:36.541 --> 00:05:40.833
remained?

95
00:05:40.833 --> 00:05:43.958
When you do not feed your guests,

96
00:05:43.958 --> 00:05:46.333
when you forget the prayer

97
00:05:46.333 --> 00:05:49.125
but remember to take a photograph,

98
00:05:49.125 --> 00:05:51.708
when your mind is on results

99
00:05:51.708 --> 00:05:54.208
and not on faith –

100
00:05:54.208 --> 00:05:57.416
then your yajna turns from sattvic

101
00:05:57.416 --> 00:06:00.791
to rajasic or tamasic.

102
00:06:00.791 --> 00:06:03.208
What truly matters

103
00:06:03.208 --> 00:06:06.583
is not only the action, but

104
00:06:06.583 --> 00:06:11.250
the feeling behind it.

105
00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:14.000
Do it with humility.

106
00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.416
Do it with faith.

107
00:06:16.416 --> 00:06:20.250
Do it with the desire for upliftment.

108
00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:23.541
Because without these, even the most sacred

109
00:06:23.541 --> 00:06:28.916
rituals remain mere performance.

110
00:06:28.916 --> 00:06:30.625
And I do not see

111
00:06:30.625 --> 00:06:33.916
only the fire of the yajna –

112
00:06:33.916 --> 00:06:38.416
I also see the flame of your heart.

113
00:06:38.416 --> 00:06:39.458
Reflect on this.

114
00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.375
When you perform a ritual at home –

115
00:06:47.375 --> 00:06:52.666
whether it is worship, a havan, or a festival –

116
00:06:52.666 --> 00:06:54.625
I want you

117
00:06:54.625 --> 00:06:59.000
to ask yourself this question:

118
00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.250
is this for me,

119
00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:03.708
or for the invited guests?

120
00:07:03.708 --> 00:07:08.041
If your preparation is focused more

121
00:07:08.041 --> 00:07:12.208
on impressing the guests,

122
00:07:12.208 --> 00:07:17.000
if the offering of worship is done
with a restless mind,

123
00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:24.666
if the prasad is kept reserved only to
give to ‘special people’

124
00:07:24.666 --> 00:07:25.791
and is not

125
00:07:25.791 --> 00:07:28.916
shared with love –

126
00:07:28.916 --> 00:07:30.875
then the yajna

127
00:07:30.875 --> 00:07:32.833
loses its soul.

128
00:07:32.833 --> 00:07:38.291
Children watch everything quietly.

129
00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:41.375
They absorb not only your rituals,

130
00:07:41.375 --> 00:07:46.375
but also your reasons.

131
00:07:46.375 --> 00:07:48.291
If they see

132
00:07:48.291 --> 00:07:51.208
that rituals are done for social prestige

133
00:07:51.208 --> 00:07:53.416
or praise,

134
00:07:53.416 --> 00:07:55.708
then they learn

135
00:07:55.708 --> 00:07:59.375
that spirituality is just a performance.

136
00:07:59.375 --> 00:08:01.750
But if they see

137
00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:02.791
that you,

138
00:08:02.791 --> 00:08:06.250
with reverence, offering with faith,

139
00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:10.291
and being compassionate, are distributing
the prasad –

140
00:08:10.291 --> 00:08:12.000
then they carry this same feeling

141
00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.250
with them throughout their lives.

142
00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:20.041
Make your home a place of sacred simplicity.

143
00:08:20.041 --> 00:08:23.041
Let sincerity breathe in your rituals,

144
00:08:23.041 --> 00:08:28.166
not performance.

145
00:08:28.166 --> 00:08:30.625
Because I do not dwell

146
00:08:30.625 --> 00:08:35.208
in the sound of loudspeakers, but

147
00:08:35.208 --> 00:08:39.458
in the peace of a grateful heart.

148
00:08:44.416 --> 00:08:46.583
Every time you give guidance

149
00:08:46.583 --> 00:08:49.375
to a new colleague,

150
00:08:49.375 --> 00:08:52.458
support a co-worker,

151
00:08:52.458 --> 00:08:55.750
or help someone in a crisis,

152
00:08:55.750 --> 00:09:00.041
you are performing a kind of yajna –

153
00:09:00.041 --> 00:09:04.791
by sacrificing your time, effort, or convenience.

154
00:09:04.791 --> 00:09:09.708
But I want you to pay attention –

155
00:09:09.708 --> 00:09:13.375
how are you doing this?

156
00:09:13.375 --> 00:09:17.625
If you help without any selfishness, without

157
00:09:17.666 --> 00:09:18.541
expecting

158
00:09:18.541 --> 00:09:26.000
appreciation, and only because it is right,

159
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.958
then your actions are sattvic.

160
00:09:29.958 --> 00:09:33.416
This uplifts you and others.

161
00:09:33.416 --> 00:09:37.833
But if you expect credit, promotion,

162
00:09:37.833 --> 00:09:40.000
or some other benefit

163
00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:43.541
in return for the help –

164
00:09:43.541 --> 00:09:47.000
then it becomes rajasic,

165
00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.625
and binds you in the net

166
00:09:49.625 --> 00:09:51.208
of expectations.

167
00:09:51.208 --> 00:09:55.000
And if you help

168
00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:57.875
carelessly, uncomfortably,

169
00:09:57.875 --> 00:10:00.000
or only to make a show –

170
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.791
while disliking it from within,

171
00:10:03.791 --> 00:10:08.000
then it becomes tamasic.

172
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:12.708
Not every sacrifice has the same result.

173
00:10:12.708 --> 00:10:16.708
The very same action, when done
with a different intention,

174
00:10:16.708 --> 00:10:19.458
gives a different fruit.

175
00:10:19.458 --> 00:10:20.875
At the workplace,

176
00:10:20.875 --> 00:10:25.000
doing good alone is not enough –

177
00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.750
be sincere as well.

178
00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:31.208
When your help is calm,

179
00:10:31.208 --> 00:10:35.000
thoughtful, and selfless,

180
00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:38.708
then it purifies not only the work,

181
00:10:38.708 --> 00:10:42.416
but also that person.
